//! Workspace HTTP admission and coordination of domain resource operations.
//!
//! The catalog dispatcher acquires a Workspace lifecycle lease and verifies a signing
//! proof or human actor before entering the inner router. Proof verification precedes
//! resource lock waits; a deleting Workspace rejects reads too. Accepted handlers are
//! not reauthenticated merely because the proof expires. Subsequent resource/provider
//! operations follow their owners' current constraints.
//!
//! Shared Worker admission lives in worker_operations; deletion draining lives in
//! workspace_admission. Generated contract routers and registered WS routes define
//! production entry points. Test helpers do not imply unauthenticated production routes.
//!
//! # Tickets and Orchestrators
//!
//! Ticket case judgments, assignment handling, operational delivery/start evidence and Worker
//! lifecycle are separate authorities. Open is not queued; closed need not mean fulfilled. Case
//! judgment requires no universal Repository/MR approval gate and handling done is not closure.
//! Current authenticated role/source constraints govern mutations, never model role text.
//!
//! Assign commits delegation and input origin before notification. Startup, create/replacement,
//! accepted Restore and Running-to-Idle attention use the same durable pending-input scan; waiting
//! alone and subscription snapshots are not new inputs. Clear/reissue/close fence old inputs;
//! reopen alone revives no work rights. Runtime acceptance is not model processing or progress.
//! Runtime spawning, Workdir links and actual work claims keep their own durable guards.
//! This coordinates notifications, not a general event queue or worktree layout policy.

